(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-forms/src/tools.asl#checkerRows" :text "known divergence from aslForms.py: checker names come from the tree's types.asl text (checkerNames/checkerBuiltins below), but each name's signature comes from ty/builtinSig, the asl-checker/types module linked into this binary, not from parsing that same tree text. Python re-derives both name and signature from the tree's types.asl on every call. The two agree only while a tree's types.asl matches the linked checker; knowParityTest cases 54,55,57-60 pin types.asl at formsPin for exactly this reason, and a later signature change to one of those builtins needs tests/parity/forms/know.asn regenerated (asl-host run tests/parity/forms/knowGen.asl) or this suite goes red. The linked checker is authoritative for signatures because re-parsing a foreign tree's source for type information the running binary already carries would be the tail reasoning about its own head")
